            SDATA Editor, v1.2 Written by Dotoran of Frontiers!
============================================================================

 NEW: In this version, the values are placed back into CNet's Memory, as
 in :   well as being saved to disk, so you NO LONGER HAVE TO REBOOT CNET
v1.2:   after changing the values.
    : A new option to "ReCalculate" the values was added. If you suspect
    :   the validity of the values stored in this file, but are not sure of
    :   what the CORRECT values SHOULD be, then try recalculating them. The
    :   program will scan through all available information in an attempt
    :   to calculate the correct values. You'll be asked if you wish to use
    :   the calculated values, before being taken back to the main screen,
    :   upon which you'd have to use the "S"ave command to officially use
    :   these new values.

    The majority of the actual docs are included within the file itself, so
I won't restate them here.

    This is an Arexx SYSOP-ONLY file, and should be placed in your PROTECTED
pfile directory(possibly the same one that houses "count","missing",etc...)

    This file will allow you to ALTER the contents of your "bbs.sdata" file
in your SYSDATA: directory. Among other values stored in this file, you will
find the TOTAL SYSTEM CALLS variable. I saw numerous posts on Future World
asking if editing of this value was possible, but I saw no one doing anything
about it, so I wrote this program.

    As a precaution, this file will make a copy of your "bbs.sdata" file,
just in case something gets messed up. The backup copy is named:

                    SYSDATA:bbs.sdata.bkup

    ...and will NOT be deleted when the file exits. It doesn't take much
room(only 20 bytes or so), so I would suggest leaving it there until you
are sure your NEW values are working properly.

    Although editing of the other variables will probably never occur, I
included them here for completeness.

